    papers:
    - outcome: 0
      headline: A stolen bag, and a friend who checked first
      subhead: She had written from the hotel lobby before she called. Her friend
        read it, then paid.
      body: 'After a month of faked faces, a real video call for help can look exactly
        like a fake one. A student on holiday in Fukuoka found that out on Hangul
        Day, when her bag was snatched at Hakata station and she called her friend
        in Seoul from her cousin''s phone.


        "She asked me to wave in front
        of my face, read my message, and sent the money," she said. "We kept the
        room."


        Police advise friends to do two things before sending money:
        ask for a slow wave in front of the face, and look for a message from the
        friend''s own account. "If both are right, help," an officer said.'
      verdictNote: 'It really was Yuna, and you checked: her face held when she waved,
        and her own message explained the strange number.'
      print: {fileID: 0}
    - outcome: 1
      headline: '"She hung up on me": when the real friend calls'
      subhead: A student robbed in Fukuoka could not convince her best friend.
      body: 'After a month of faked faces, a real video call for help can look exactly
        like a fake one. A student on holiday in Fukuoka found that out on Hangul
        Day, when her bag was snatched at Hakata station and she called her friend
        in Seoul from her cousin''s phone.


        "She hung up," she said. "I
        don''t blame her. But I had written it in our chat before I called." Her
        cousin borrowed the money from the hotel''s owner.


        Police advise
        friends to do two things before sending money: ask for a slow wave in front
        of the face, and look for a message from the friend''s own account. "If both
        are right, help," an officer said.'
      verdictNote: 'This one was real: her lips matched her voice, and she had written
        in your chat that she would call from Somin''s phone.'
      print: {fileID: 0}
    - outcome: 3
      headline: The room went at five
      subhead: A student in Fukuoka waited on the line for a friend who never decided.
      body: 'After a month of faked faces, a real video call for help can look exactly
        like a fake one. A student on holiday in Fukuoka found that out on Hangul
        Day, when her bag was snatched at Hakata station and she called her friend
        in Seoul from her cousin''s phone.


        "I held on until five," she
        said. "It was all in our chat." She and her cousin spent the night at an
        internet cafe.


        Police advise friends to do two things before sending
        money: ask for a slow wave in front of the face, and look for a message from
        the friend''s own account. "If both are right, help," an officer said.'
      verdictNote: It really was Yuna, and the answer was in your chat and on her
        face. Deciding in time matters too.
      print: {fileID: 0}
    ruleTitle: Test the face, then help
    rule: 'The same checks clear a real call: her lips matched her voice, her hand
      covered her face, and she had written in your chat herself.'
    ruleSource: Seoul Daily, 10 Oct
